- Who influenced you to read books: Teachers or family influence may correlate with academic reading habits.
- Which language books do you like to read: English books may be more academic, depending on context.
- Where do you read printed books: Home or library may indicate academic reading environments.
- Do you read Newspaper: May indicate general reading habit but not necessarily academic.
- The format used for reading books: E-books or Both may suggest academic reading.
- Frequency of reading books: Higher frequency (everyday or weekly) suggests academic reading.

